The legal texts in this repository are official texts of the Republic of Haiti: the Constitution of 29 March 1987 and its
amendment (Le Moniteur, 19 June 2012), codes, laws, decrees and orders.

Official texts are not protected by copyright in Haiti. The Decree of 12 October 2005 on Copyright (Le Moniteur no. 23,
9 March 2006), Article 5, says:

  "La protection prévue par le présent Décret ne s'étend pas : 1.- aux textes officiels de nature législative, administrative ou
  judiciaire, ni à leurs traductions officielles; ..."

Sources of the bytes, and their terms:
- Ministère de l'Économie et des Finances (https://www.mef.gouv.ht/) and Direction générale du Budget (https://budget.gouv.ht/):
  copies of Le Moniteur published by the State; official texts (Decree of 2005, art. 5).
- Digithèque de matériaux juridiques et politiques (MJP), Université de Perpignan (https://mjp.univ-perp.fr/constit/ht1987.htm,
  ht2011.htm): third-party copy of the Constitution; the host's own commentary is not reproduced.
- CEPAL Gender Equality Observatory (https://oig.cepal.org/sites/default/files/2003_codtravail_hti.pdf): third-party copy of the
  Code du travail.
- FAOLEX, FAO Legal Office (https://faolex.fao.org/): third-party copies; FAO terms allow non-commercial reuse with
  acknowledgement (https://www.fao.org/contact-us/terms/db-terms-of-use/en/). Each such commit carries
  "Source-status: secondary copy (FAOLEX, <url>)".
- haitijustice.com, Centre de recherche et d'information juridiques (CRIJ); the site has closed and the copies are read from the
  Internet Archive's Wayback Machine (https://web.archive.org/). Its notice allowed reuse "sous réserve du respect de la mention
  de la source [et] de l'intégrité des documents reproduits": the source is named in every commit ("Source-status: secondary
  copy (haitijustice.com ...)") and the text is not altered beyond splitting it into articles.

The arrangement of this repository, its tables, commit messages and tools are by Lexifina and are dedicated to the public domain
under CC0 1.0 Universal (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). This repository is not legal advice and not an
official publication.
